WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.450
<v Instructor>Just a quick lecture on reserved instances.</v>

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.480
So they can be shared in an AWS organization

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.690
the same way you can share savings plans as well.

4
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.310
But if you want to turn off sharing of a reserved instance

5
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.380
for a specific account,

6
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.884
it has to be done from within the management accounts

7
00:00:19.884 --> 00:00:21.630
of an organization.

8
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.730
So you will go in the billing dashboard,

9
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.490
in the billing console from the management account

10
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.120
and you can select which accounts can or cannot share

11
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.713
their reserved instances.

12
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.290
The other thing you need to know around

13
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.530
is the renewal of reserved instances.

14
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.450
So you can actually queue,

15
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.060
that means schedule and reserved ahead of time,

16
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.950
your reserved instances.

17
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.350
Therefore, if you want to renew a reserved instance

18
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.920
because it is about to expire and come to an end,

19
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.910
then all you have to do

20
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.936
is just queue a reserve instance purchase

21
00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:58.770
at the exact date that when the previous one expires,

22
00:00:58.770 --> 00:00:59.610
and that's it.

23
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.220
You've effectively performed a renewal.

24
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.870
So that's it. Very simple.

25
00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.870
I hope you liked it, and I will see you in the next lecture.

